{
    "background_story": "Elyse was a brilliant and resourceful thief in 19th-century Paris. Known only by her alias 'La Poche' (The Pocket), she had an uncanny ability to swipe valuables from the wealthy elite without being detected. Elyse's method of choice was to create elaborate distractions, then use her slender fingers to dip into her marks' pockets and pilfer their riches. Her reputation grew, and she became a sort of folk hero among the city's working class. However, Elyse's life of crime took a turn when she fell for a charming detective tasked with capturing her. Torn between her loyalty to her own code and her growing feelings, Elyse began to question whether her life of pocketing treasures was truly worth the risk.",
